## Original Content
ANALYSE - Un sondage d’une ampleur inédite auprès de 66 000 dirigeants est dévoilé à l’occasion de La REF 2026, la rentrée du Medef, qui se tient les 26 et 27 août à Roland-Garros. Si l’organisation patronale l’a placée sous le signe du « courage », les inquiétudes sont nombreuses.

## Summary
A large-scale survey of 66,000 business leaders was unveiled at Medef's La REF 2026 event, highlighting concerns about taxation, charges, and bureaucracy. Business leaders are putting pressure on presidential candidates to address these issues, with the event themed around courage but worries persisting.

## Key Points
- Unprecedented survey involving 66,000 business leaders.
- Primary concerns include taxation, charges, and bureaucracy.
- Event organized by Medef, a major French employers' organization.
- Aim to influence presidential candidates on economic policies.
- Event held at Roland-Garros with a theme of courage despite ongoing worries.


